{"id":"mahabharata-12-056","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":56,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 56 · The king's conduct","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira bows to Krishna and Bhishma and asks the duties of a king. Bhishma tells him that a king should be mild but not too mild, and that he should know his counsellors and ministers by their tests, and describes the faults to be avoided.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೃಷ್ಣ, ಭೀಷ್ಮರಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸಿ ರಾಜಧರ್ಮ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಾಜ ಮೃದುವಾಗಿರಬೇಕು ಆದರೆ ತೀರಾ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮಂತ್ರಿಗಳನ್ನು ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ ತಿಳಿಯಬೇಕು, ತಪ್ಪಿಸಬೇಕಾದ ದೋಷಗಳನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कृष्ण और भीष्म को प्रणाम कर राजधर्म पूछते हैं। भीष्म बताते हैं कि राजा मृदु हो पर अधिक नहीं, मन्त्रियों को परीक्षा से परखे, और वे त्यागने योग्य दोष गिनाते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు కృష్ణ భీష్ములకు నమస్కరించి రాజధర్మం అడుగుతాడు. రాజు మృదువుగా ఉండాలి కానీ అతి కాదని, మంత్రులను పరీక్షించి తెలుసుకోవాలని, విడవవలసిన దోషాలను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் கண்ணனையும் பீஷ்மரையும் வணங்கி ராஜதர்மத்தைக் கேட்கிறார். மன்னன் மென்மையாக இருக்க வேண்டும் ஆனால் மிகையாக அல்ல, அமைச்சரைச் சோதித்து அறிய வேண்டும் என்றும் தவிர்க்க வேண்டிய குறைகளையும் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ കൃഷ്ണനെയും ഭീഷ്മരെയും നമസ്കരിച്ച് രാജധർമ്മം ചോദിക്കുന്നു. രാജാവ് മൃദുവായിരിക്കണം, എന്നാൽ അധികം മൃദുവായിരിക്കരുതെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ഉപദേഷ്ടാക്കളെയും മന്ത്രിമാരെയും പരീക്ഷിച്ച് അറിയണമെന്നും, ഒഴിവാക്കേണ്ട കുറവുകൾ വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.56; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रणिपत्य हृषीकेशमभिवाद्य पितामहम् ।\nअनुमान्य गुरून्सर्वान्पर्यपृच्छद्युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bowing to Hrishikesha, saluting the grandfather and honoring all the elders, Yudhishthira questioned Bhishma."}},{"n":2,"text":"राज्यं वै परमो धर्म इति धर्मविदो विदुः ।\nमहान्तमेतं भारं च मन्ये तद्ब्रूहि पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know dharma say that kingship is the highest duty, and I think it a very heavy burden; so tell me of it, king."}},{"n":3,"text":"राजधर्मान्विशेषेण कथयस्व पितामह ।\nसर्वस्य जीवलोकस्य राजधर्माः परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, speak especially of the duties of kings, for the duties of kings are the final support of the whole world of the living."}},{"n":4,"text":"त्रिवर्गोऽत्र समासक्तो राजधर्मेषु कौरव ।\nमोक्षधर्मश्च विस्पष्टः सकलोऽत्र समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here, Kaurava, the three aims of life are bound up in the duties of kings, and the whole path of liberation is plainly contained here too."}},{"n":5,"text":"यथा हि रश्मयोऽश्वस्य द्विरदस्याङ्कुशो यथा ।\nनरेन्द्रधर्मो लोकस्य तथा प्रग्रहणं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As reins are to a horse and the goad to an elephant, so the rule of a king is remembered as the restraint of the world."}},{"n":6,"text":"अत्र वै संप्रमूढे तु धर्मे राजर्षिसेविते ।\nलोकस्य संस्था न भवेत्सर्वं च व्याकुलं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If this dharma practised by royal sages becomes confused, the order of the world will not stand and everything will fall into disorder."}},{"n":7,"text":"उदयन्हि यथा सूर्यो नाशयत्यासुरं तमः ।\nराजधर्मास्तथालोक्यामाक्षिपन्त्यशुभां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the rising sun destroys the darkness of the asuras, so the duties of kings remove an unlucky and miserable fate from the world."}},{"n":8,"text":"तदग्रे राजधर्माणामर्थतत्त्वं पितामह ।\nप्रब्रूहि भरतश्रेष्ठ त्वं हि बुद्धिमतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, grandfather, best of the Bharatas, first tell the true meaning of the duties of kings, for you are the best of the wise."}},{"n":9,"text":"आगमश्च परस्त्वत्तः सर्वेषां नः परंतप ।\nभवन्तं हि परं बुद्धौ वासुदेवोऽभिमन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the supreme source of learning for all of us, tormentor of foes, and Vasudeva too holds you as supreme in understanding."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"नमो धर्माय महते नमः कृष्णाय वेधसे ।\nब्राह्मणेभ्यो नमस्कृत्य धर्मान्वक्ष्यामि शाश्वतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Homage to great dharma, homage to Krishna the creator; having bowed to the brahmins I shall speak the eternal duties."}},{"n":11,"text":"शृणु कार्त्स्न्येन मत्तस्त्वं राजधर्मान्युधिष्ठिर ।\nनिरुच्यमानान्नियतो यच्चान्यदभिवाञ्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen to me in full, Yudhishthira, as I set out the duties of kings, steady in mind, and whatever else you wish to know."}},{"n":12,"text":"आदावेव कुरुश्रेष्ठ राज्ञा रञ्जनकाम्यया ।\nदेवतानां द्विजानां च वर्तितव्यं यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"First of all, best of the Kurus, a king should deal with the gods and brahmins in the proper way, wishing to please them."}},{"n":13,"text":"दैवतान्यर्चयित्वा हि ब्राह्मणांश्च कुरूद्वह ।\nआनृण्यं याति धर्मस्य लोकेन च स मान्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For having worshipped the deities and brahmins, bearer of the Kuru line, he becomes free of his debt to dharma and is honored by the world."}},{"n":14,"text":"उत्थाने च सदा पुत्र प्रयतेथा युधिष्ठिर ।\nन ह्युत्थानमृते दैवं राज्ञामर्थप्रसिद्धये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear son Yudhishthira, always strive in effort; without effort, fate alone does not bring success in the aims of kings."}},{"n":15,"text":"साधारणं द्वयं ह्येतद्दैवमुत्थानमेव च ।\nपौरुषं हि परं मन्ये दैवं निश्चित्यमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fate and effort are both common to all; I hold human effort to be the greater, and fate is said to be something merely inferred."}},{"n":16,"text":"विपन्ने च समारम्भे संतापं मा स्म वै कृथाः ।\nघटते विनयस्तात राज्ञामेष नयः परः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If an undertaking fails, do not grieve; dear child, to keep trying with discipline is the highest policy for kings."}},{"n":17,"text":"न हि सत्यादृते किंचिद्राज्ञां वै सिद्धिकारणम् ।\nसत्ये हि राजा निरतः प्रेत्य चेह च नन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For kings nothing causes success except truth; a king devoted to truth rejoices here and hereafter."}},{"n":18,"text":"ऋषीणामपि राजेन्द्र सत्यमेव परं धनम् ।\nतथा राज्ञः परं सत्यान्नान्यद्विश्वासकारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even for sages, king of kings, truth alone is the highest wealth, and for a king nothing but truth is the basis of trust."}},{"n":19,"text":"गुणवाञ्शीलवान्दान्तो मृदुर्धर्म्यो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nसुदर्शः स्थूललक्ष्यश्च न भ्रश्येत सदा श्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who is virtuous, well-behaved, self-controlled, gentle, righteous, master of his senses, far-sighted and generous in sight will never fall from prosperity."}},{"n":20,"text":"आर्जवं सर्वकार्येषु श्रयेथाः कुरुनन्दन ।\nपुनर्नयविचारेण त्रयीसंवरणेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delight of the Kurus, rely on uprightness in all affairs, joined with careful reflection on policy and with the keeping of the three Vedas secure."}},{"n":21,"text":"मृदुर्हि राजा सततं लङ्घ्यो भवति सर्वशः ।\nतीक्ष्णाच्चोद्विजते लोकस्तस्मादुभयमाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"A gentle king is always overrun on every side, while the world is frightened of a harsh one; so practise both."}},{"n":22,"text":"अदण्ड्याश्चैव ते नित्यं विप्राः स्युर्ददतां वर ।\nभूतमेतत्परं लोके ब्राह्मणा नाम भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of givers, brahmins should always be exempt from punishment; brahmins, descendant of Bharata, are the highest being in the world."}},{"n":23,"text":"मनुना चापि राजेन्द्र गीतौ श्लोकौ महात्मना ।\nधर्मेषु स्वेषु कौरव्य हृदि तौ कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"King of kings, the great Manu also sang two verses; you should take them to heart among your own duties, descendant of Kuru."}},{"n":24,"text":"अद्भ्योऽग्निर्ब्रह्मतः क्षत्रमश्मनो लोहमुत्थितम् ।\nतेषां सर्वत्रगं तेजः स्वासु योनिषु शाम्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire arose from water, the kshatra from the brahmin, and iron from stone; their all-penetrating force is quenched in their own sources."}},{"n":25,"text":"अयो हन्ति यदाश्मानमग्निश्चापोऽभिपद्यते ।\nब्रह्म च क्षत्रियो द्वेष्टि तदा सीदन्ति ते त्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When iron strikes stone, fire strikes water, or a kshatriya turns against a brahmin, all three of them come to ruin."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतज्ज्ञात्वा महाराज नमस्या एव ते द्विजाः ।\nभौमं ब्रह्म द्विजश्रेष्ठा धारयन्ति शमान्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this, great king, those twice-born are to be revered; best of brahmins, tranquil, they bear on earth the brahmin power."}},{"n":27,"text":"एवं चैव नरव्याघ्र लोकतन्त्रविघातकाः ।\nनिग्राह्या एव सततं बाहुभ्यां ये स्युरीदृशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise, tiger among men, those who harm the order of the world are always to be restrained by force of arm."}},{"n":28,"text":"श्लोकौ चोशनसा गीतौ पुरा तात महर्षिणा ।\nतौ निबोध महाप्राज्ञ त्वमेकाग्रमना नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two verses were also sung long ago by the great sage Ushanas; hear them, wise king, with a single mind."}},{"n":29,"text":"उद्यम्य शस्त्रमायान्तमपि वेदान्तगं रणे ।\nनिगृह्णीयात्स्वधर्मेण धर्मापेक्षी नरेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who looks to dharma should restrain by his own duty even a master of the Vedanta who comes against him in battle with a raised weapon."}},{"n":30,"text":"विनश्यमानं धर्मं हि यो रक्षति स धर्मवित् ।\nन तेन भ्रूणहा स स्यान्मन्युस्तं मनुमृच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who protects dharma as it is perishing knows dharma; he does not become a killer of a brahmin by it, for his anger passes to Manu."}},{"n":31,"text":"एवं चैव नरश्रेष्ठ रक्ष्या एव द्विजातयः ।\nस्वपराद्धानपि हि तान्विषयान्ते समुत्सृजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise, best of men, the twice-born are to be protected; even when they offend against him, he should banish them to the edge of his realm."}},{"n":32,"text":"अभिशस्तमपि ह्येषां कृपायीत विशां पते ।\nब्रह्मघ्ने गुरुतल्पे च भ्रूणहत्ये तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Show compassion even to one among them who is condemned, lord of the people, for a brahmin who has killed a brahmin, defiled a teacher's bed or killed an embryo,"}},{"n":33,"text":"राजद्विष्टे च विप्रस्य विषयान्ते विसर्जनम् ।\nविधीयते न शारीरं भयमेषां कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"or who has offended the king: banishment to the border of the realm is the ordained penalty; they are never to suffer bodily harm."}},{"n":34,"text":"दयिताश्च नरास्ते स्युर्नित्यं पुरुषसत्तम ।\nन कोशः परमो ह्यन्यो राज्ञां पुरुषसंचयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the people always be dear to you, best of men, for no treasury is greater for kings than a gathering of men."}},{"n":35,"text":"दुर्गेषु च महाराज षट्सु ये शास्त्रनिश्चिताः ।\nसर्वेषु तेषु मन्यन्ते नरदुर्गं सुदुस्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the six kinds of fort fixed in the scriptures, great king, they hold the fortress of men to be the hardest of all to cross."}},{"n":36,"text":"तस्मान्नित्यं दया कार्या चातुर्वर्ण्ये विपश्चिता ।\nधर्मात्मा सत्यवाक्चैव राजा रञ्जयति प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore the wise king should always show kindness to all four classes; a righteous, truthful king pleases his subjects."}},{"n":37,"text":"न च क्षान्तेन ते भाव्यं नित्यं पुरुषसत्तम ।\nअधर्म्यो हि मृदू राजा क्षमावानिव कुञ्जरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, you must not be always forgiving; a king who is soft and forgiving like an elephant is unrighteous."}},{"n":38,"text":"बार्हस्पत्ये च शास्त्रे वै श्लोका विनियताः पुरा ।\nअस्मिन्नर्थे महाराज तन्मे निगदतः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago verses were laid down in the science of Brihaspati on this matter, great king; hear them as I recite."}},{"n":39,"text":"क्षममाणं नृपं नित्यं नीचः परिभवेज्जनः ।\nहस्तियन्ता गजस्येव शिर एवारुरुक्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A lowly person will scorn a king who is always forbearing, as an elephant driver wishes to climb onto an elephant's head."}},{"n":40,"text":"तस्मान्नैव मृदुर्नित्यं तीक्ष्णो वापि भवेन्नृपः ।\nवसन्तेऽर्क इव श्रीमान्न शीतो न च घर्मदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore a king should be neither always gentle nor always harsh; like the radiant sun in spring, he should be neither cold nor scorching."}},{"n":41,"text":"प्रत्यक्षेणानुमानेन तथौपम्योपदेशतः ।\nपरीक्ष्यास्ते महाराज स्वे परे चैव सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By direct perception, inference, and teaching by comparison, great king, you should always examine your own side and the other."}},{"n":42,"text":"व्यसनानि च सर्वाणि त्यजेथा भूरिदक्षिण ।\nन चैव न प्रयुञ्जीत सङ्गं तु परिवर्जयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Open-handed one, give up every vice; do not indulge them, and avoid attachment altogether."}},{"n":43,"text":"नित्यं हि व्यसनी लोके परिभूतो भवत्युत ।\nउद्वेजयति लोकं चाप्यतिद्वेषी महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a man who is always given to vice is despised in the world, and a king who hates too much torments the world."}},{"n":44,"text":"भवितव्यं सदा राज्ञा गर्भिणीसहधर्मिणा ।\nकारणं च महाराज शृणु येनेदमिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should always act like a pregnant woman who shares her duty; hear, great king, the reason for this."}},{"n":45,"text":"यथा हि गर्भिणी हित्वा स्वं प्रियं मनसोऽनुगम् ।\nगर्भस्य हितमाधत्ते तथा राज्ञाप्यसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a pregnant woman gives up what she loves and her mind desires, for the good of the child, so a king too undoubtedly"}},{"n":46,"text":"वर्तितव्यं कुरुश्रेष्ठ नित्यं धर्मानुवर्तिना ।\nस्वं प्रियं समभित्यज्य यद्यल्लोकहितं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"should always act following dharma, giving up what he likes whenever it is for the good of the world."}},{"n":47,"text":"न संत्याज्यं च ते धैर्यं कदाचिदपि पाण्डव ।\nधीरस्य स्पष्टदण्डस्य न ह्याज्ञा प्रतिहन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandava, you must never abandon steadiness; for the steady king whose punishment is clear, his command is never broken."}},{"n":48,"text":"परिहासश्च भृत्यैस्ते न नित्यं वदतां वर ।\nकर्तव्यो राजशार्दूल दोषमत्र हि मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of speakers, tiger among kings, you should not make a habit of joking with your servants; hear the fault in it from me."}},{"n":49,"text":"अवमन्यन्ति भर्तारं संहर्षादुपजीविनः ।\nस्वे स्थाने न च तिष्ठन्ति लङ्घयन्ति हि तद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dependents grow bold and look down on their master; they do not keep to their own place and they transgress his word."}},{"n":50,"text":"प्रेष्यमाणा विकल्पन्ते गुह्यं चाप्यनुयुञ्जते ।\nअयाच्यं चैव याचन्तेऽभोज्यान्याहारयन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sent on errands they dither, they pry into secrets, they ask for what should not be asked and take food not fit to take."}},{"n":51,"text":"क्रुध्यन्ति परिदीप्यन्ति भूमिमध्यासतेऽस्य च ।\nउत्कोचैर्वञ्चनाभिश्च कार्याण्यनुविहन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They get angry, they flare up, they sit on the ground where he sits, and by bribes and deceptions they spoil his affairs."}},{"n":52,"text":"जर्जरं चास्य विषयं कुर्वन्ति प्रतिरूपकैः ।\nस्त्रीरक्षिभिश्च सज्जन्ते तुल्यवेषा भवन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They ruin his realm with counterfeits, they become attached to the guardians of the women, and they wear the same dress as he does."}},{"n":53,"text":"वातं च ष्ठीवनं चैव कुर्वते चास्य संनिधौ ।\nनिर्लज्जा नरशार्दूल व्याहरन्ति च तद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In his presence they pass wind and spit, shameless, tiger among men, and they repeat his words."}},{"n":54,"text":"हयं वा दन्तिनं वापि रथं नृपतिसंमतम् ।\nअधिरोहन्त्यनादृत्य हर्षुले पार्थिवे मृदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They mount the king's favored horse, elephant or chariot without regard, when the king is joking and soft."}},{"n":55,"text":"इदं ते दुष्करं राजन्निदं ते दुर्विचेष्टितम् ।\nइत्येवं सुहृदो नाम ब्रुवन्ति परिषद्गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So-called friends in the assembly say, \"This is hard for you, king; this is badly done by you.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"क्रुद्धे चास्मिन्हसन्त्येव न च हृष्यन्ति पूजिताः ।\nसंघर्षशीलाश्च सदा भवन्त्यन्योन्यकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he is angry they only laugh, and when honored they are not pleased; they are always quarrelsome with one another over trifles."}},{"n":57,"text":"विस्रंसयन्ति मन्त्रं च विवृण्वन्ति च दुष्कृतम् ।\nलीलया चैव कुर्वन्ति सावज्ञास्तस्य शासनम् ।\nअलंकरणभोज्यं च तथा स्नानानुलेपनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They leak out his counsel and reveal his wrongs; they carry out his orders playfully and with contempt, and they take his ornaments, food, bathing and unguents for themselves."}},{"n":58,"text":"हेलमाना नरव्याघ्र स्वस्थास्तस्योपशृण्वते ।\nनिन्दन्ति स्वानधीकारान्संत्यजन्ति च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tiger among men, they disdain him, listen to him idly, find fault with their own duties, and abandon them, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":59,"text":"न वृत्त्या परितुष्यन्ति राजदेयं हरन्ति च ।\nक्रीडितुं तेन चेच्छन्ति ससूत्रेणेव पक्षिणा ।\nअस्मत्प्रणेयो राजेति लोके चैव वदन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are not satisfied with their pay, they steal what is due to the king, and they want to play with him as one plays with a bird on a string; and they say among the people, \"The king is led by us.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"एते चैवापरे चैव दोषाः प्रादुर्भवन्त्युत ।\nनृपतौ मार्दवोपेते हर्षुले च युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and other faults arise, Yudhishthira, with a king who is gentle and fond of joking."}}]}]}